WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.540
10,000 Ships is the name of one of the upcoming
Game of Thrones prequels and it's main character

00:00:05.540 --> 00:00:07.200
is Princess Nymeria.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:12.670
Set 1,000 years before the events of Game
of Thrones, the series tells the story of

00:00:12.670 --> 00:00:19.640
warrior-queen Nymeria of Ny Sar was who led
the Rhoynar refugees from Essos to Dorne following

00:00:19.640 --> 00:00:23.220
their defeat by Valyrian and their 300 dragons.

00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:29.229
She’s an ancestor of House Martell and House
Dayne, and is seen as the founder of Dorne

00:00:29.229 --> 00:00:32.189
as a unified realm under Martell rule.

00:00:32.189 --> 00:00:37.640
Through the marriage of Myriah Martell to
King Daeron II, Nymeria is also an ancestor

00:00:37.640 --> 00:00:39.580
of House Targaryen.

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:45.220
After the Rhoyne was conquered by the Valyrian
Freehold, Nymeria led the Rhoynar to Dorne,

00:00:45.220 --> 00:00:49.380
where she took Lord Mors Martell of Sandship
as her husband.

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:55.240
After years of war and conquest, House Nymeros
Martell established supremacy over Dorne,

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:59.650
with Nymeria ruling for well over two decades
as the Princess of Dorne.

00:00:59.650 --> 00:01:05.219
Through Nymeria's rule, the Dornish adopted
many Rhoynish customs and laws that remain

00:01:05.219 --> 00:01:06.679
to this day.

00:01:06.679 --> 00:01:09.179
Princess Nymeria was said to be beautiful.

00:01:09.179 --> 00:01:14.350
Described by Maester Yandel as strong-willed
and indomitable, Princess Nymeria was said

00:01:14.350 --> 00:01:17.130
to have cunning, skill, and wisdom.

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:21.859
Although Nymeria is remembered as a "warrior
queen", and in songs is said to have been

00:01:21.859 --> 00:01:25.289
a witch, neither statement is true.

00:01:25.289 --> 00:01:30.479
Nymeria is remembered as a warrior-queen,
although she actually was not a warrior herself,

00:01:30.479 --> 00:01:33.380
in the sense of carrying and wielding weapons.

00:01:33.380 --> 00:01:38.400
She was considered a warrior for being a cunning
military strategist and commander of armies

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.459
(comparable to how in his later years Tywin
Lannister was considered a dangerous war-leader,

00:01:44.459 --> 00:01:47.279
without actually wielding his own sword anymore).

00:01:47.279 --> 00:01:53.749
At the time of the Rhoynish Wars, Nymeria
ruled in Ny Sar, where she had a palace.

00:01:53.749 --> 00:01:57.960
The Rhoynar once lived in city-states along
the Rhoyne River.

00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:04.060
About a thousand years ago (perhaps 700 years
before the Targaryen Conquest), the Rhoynar

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:09.530
were on the verge of being conquered by the
expanding power of the Valyrian Freehold and

00:02:09.530 --> 00:02:10.950
its dragons.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:17.240
During the Second Spice War, Prince Garin
united the Rhoynar nobility in a grand alliance

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.500
against the Valyrian Freehold.

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:24.670
Only Princess Nymeria spoke against him, warning
the other princes that they could not win

00:02:24.670 --> 00:02:25.670
the war.

00:02:25.670 --> 00:02:31.570
However, other princes shouted her down and
joined their strength to Prince Garin, and

00:02:31.570 --> 00:02:35.950
even Nymeria's own warriors were eager to
join his cause.

00:02:35.950 --> 00:02:42.110
Despite her own reluctance, Nymeria found
herself forced to join the great alliance.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:48.180
The war began a thousand years ago when three
dragon-lords from the Valyrian Freehold joined

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:52.450
Volantis in destroying the Rhoynish port Sarhoy
on the Summer Sea.

00:02:52.450 --> 00:02:58.000
The Rhoynar responded by uniting under Prince
Garin, the wonder of the Rhoyne who temporarily

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:00.260
made Valyria tremble.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:07.360
Garin led a Rhoynish army of 250,000, which
conquered Selhorys, Valysar, and Volon Therys,

00:03:07.360 --> 00:03:12.360
where they defeated three dragons with Rhoynish
water wizards.

00:03:12.360 --> 00:03:17.680
The alarmed Volantenes sought help from Valyria
itself, and the dragonlords' response sealed

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:19.580
the fate of the Rhoynar.

00:03:19.580 --> 00:03:25.550
Despite Prince Garin's initial success against
the Freehold, the Valyrians responded by sending

00:03:25.550 --> 00:03:28.920
three hundred dragons against the Rhoynar.

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:32.300
Garin's host was shattered and the prince
was captured.

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:38.370
Upriver at Ny Sar, Princess Nymeria learned
of Garin's defeat and the enslavement of her

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:42.660
people, and she knew that her city awaited
the same fate.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:47.700
In response, she gathered every ship that
remained upon the Rhoyne and filled them with

00:03:47.700 --> 00:03:53.180
as many women and children as they could carry—most
of the men had perished alongside Garin's

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.180
host.

00:03:54.180 --> 00:03:59.170
Rhoynar women were trained to fight as much
as Rhoynar men so Nymeria's army was still

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:00.460
a great force.

00:04:00.460 --> 00:04:07.100
While legends often claim that Nymeria commanded
a fleet of ten thousand ships, Beldecar argues

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:12.940
in his History of the Rhoynish Wars that the
number was inflated, perhaps by tenfold.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:18.209
While other chroniclers offer other numbers,
in truth no count was ever made.

00:04:18.209 --> 00:04:25.040
Maester Yandel agrees that Nymeria led a great
many ships, mostly river craft, skiffs, poleboats,

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:30.660
trading galleys, fishing boats, rafts, and
pleasure barges, crammed with women, children,

00:04:30.660 --> 00:04:32.170
and old men.

00:04:32.170 --> 00:04:35.190
Only one in ten was seaworthy, Beldecar insists.

00:04:35.190 --> 00:04:41.270
Nymeria led her ragged fleet down the Rhoyne,
past ruined towns and fields of corpses.

00:04:41.270 --> 00:04:46.460
To avoid Volantis and the dragonlords, Nymeria
chose an older channel and emerged into the

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:50.200
Summer Sea where the city of Sarhoy once stood.

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:55.010
The following voyage was long and terrible,
and more than a hundred ships sank in the

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.260
first storm they encountered.

00:04:57.260 --> 00:05:02.750
As many or more were taken by fear and turned
back, only to be captured by slavers out of

00:05:02.750 --> 00:05:04.110
Volantis.

00:05:04.110 --> 00:05:08.260
Others fell behind or drifted away, and were
never seen again.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:13.560
Nymeria's fleet first limped to the Basilisk
Isles, where they paused to take on fresh

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:18.730
water and provisions, only to be descended
upon by local pirate kings.

00:05:18.730 --> 00:05:23.360
The corsairs allowed the Rhoynar to settle
on the Isle of Toads in exchange for their

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:30.410
ships and thirty virgins each year for each
king as tribute, although Nymeria refused.

00:05:30.410 --> 00:05:35.860
She took her fleet to sea again, hoping to
find refuge on Sothoryos.

00:05:35.860 --> 00:05:41.180
Nymeria settled at Zamettar, while others
settled at Yeen or founded new towns.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:47.650
However, the Rhoynar did not thrive, succumbing
to disease, the dangers of the jungles, attacks

00:05:47.650 --> 00:05:50.860
from slavers, and the native population.

00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:57.060
After two new towns were sacked by slavers
and the Rhoynar settled in Yeen vanished,

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:01.750
Nymeria summoned her people back to their
ships and they set sail once again.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:06.080
Nymeria's fleet wandered the southern seas
for three years.

00:06:06.080 --> 00:06:11.270
The Rhoynar attempted to settle in Naath where
they were welcomed by its peaceful people,

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.280
but they were soon driven off by disease.

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:20.550
In the Summer Isles, the Rhoynar settled on
the uninhabited so-called "Isle of Women"

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:22.440
for more than two years.

00:06:22.440 --> 00:06:27.820
The princes of the isles refused to allow
them to settle on larger islands, fearing

00:06:27.820 --> 00:06:29.760
the wrath of the Freehold.

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:36.210
However, many soon starved for the island
was poorly soiled and yielded little food,

00:06:36.210 --> 00:06:38.910
and disease and slavers took their toll.

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:44.740
Some of the Rhoynar abandoned Nymeria to follow
a priestess named Druselka to return to their

00:06:44.740 --> 00:06:50.470
cities along the Rhoyne, only to be enslaved
or slain by their enemies.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:55.190
Finally, Nymeria turned west and the remnants
of her fleet settled in the deserts of Dorne

00:06:55.190 --> 00:07:01.680
on Westeros; the less seaworthy ships settled
the Stepstones or gave themselves up to slavers

00:07:01.680 --> 00:07:03.570
of the Free Cities.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:08.600
Nymeria and her ships finally made landfall
on the coast of Dorne, near the mouth of the

00:07:08.600 --> 00:07:13.530
river Greenblood, not far from the Sandship,
the ancient seat of House Martell.

00:07:13.530 --> 00:07:19.280
At the time of Nymeria's arrival, Dorne was
a poor land where a score of lords and petty

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:23.229
kings quarreled over rivers, wells, and fertile
water.

00:07:23.229 --> 00:07:28.770
Many viewed the Rhoynar as unwelcome invaders
who should be driven back into the sea.

00:07:28.770 --> 00:07:33.980
However, Lord Mors Martell of the Sandship
saw an opportunity in the Rhoynar—and singers

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:38.400
claim that Lord Martell also lost his heart
to the beautiful princess.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:45.010
With many trained in warfare, the Rhoynar
added their strength to Lord Martell's own,

00:07:45.010 --> 00:07:47.430
increasing his host by tenfold.

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:53.120
Mors married Nymeria, and hundreds of his
knights, squires, and bannermen wed Rhoynish

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.760
women, uniting the two people by blood.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:08:00.740
The Rhoynar also brought considerable wealth
with them and their artisans and armorers'

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:05.200
skills were far advanced than those of their
Westerosi counterparts.

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:11.860
To celebrate these unions and to ensure that
her people could not retreat to the sea again,

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:17.699
Nymeria burned her fleet, declaring her wanderings
to be at an end, though some of her people

00:08:17.699 --> 00:08:20.600
mourned the loss of their ships.

00:08:20.600 --> 00:08:26.340
Nymeria named her husband the Prince of Dorne,
declaring his dominion over all of Dorne.

00:08:26.340 --> 00:08:32.800
However, such supremacy was not an easy feat
and years of war followed, called Nymeria's

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:33.800
War.

00:08:33.800 --> 00:08:39.200
The Rhoynar and the Martells subdued one petty
king after another, and no fewer than six

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:44.260
kings were sent to the Wall to join the Night's
Watch by Nymeria and her husband.

00:08:44.260 --> 00:08:49.510
Soon, only King Yorick V Yronwood remained,
the greatest of the Dornish kings.

00:08:49.510 --> 00:08:54.540
For nine years, Nymeria and the Martells battled
against Yronwood and his bannermen.

00:08:54.540 --> 00:09:00.890
When her husband fell to Yronwood's sword
in the Third Battle of the Boneway, Nymeria

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:03.900
assumed sole command of the Martell armies.

00:09:03.900 --> 00:09:09.980
Two more years of battle followed, but Nymeria
eventually defeated Yorick V and he bent the

00:09:09.980 --> 00:09:13.660
knee to her, ensuring Martell supremacy.

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:20.310
Nymeria ruled thereafter from Sunspear, the
new seat of House Martell built around Sandship.

00:09:20.310 --> 00:09:25.820
As the Princess of Dorne, Nymeria remained
the unquestioned ruler of Dorne for almost

00:09:25.820 --> 00:09:27.860
twenty-seven years.

00:09:27.860 --> 00:09:32.890
Dorne was established as a principality, not
a kingdom, for Nymeria preferred the Rhoynish

00:09:32.890 --> 00:09:34.870
style of prince and princess.

00:09:34.870 --> 00:09:40.470
Alhough she remarried twice to Lord Uller
of Hellholt and Ser Davos Dayne of Starfall,

00:09:40.470 --> 00:09:44.440
her husbands served only as counselors and
consorts.

00:09:44.440 --> 00:09:50.490
Over the course of her long reign, Nymeria
survived a dozen assassination attempts, quelled

00:09:50.490 --> 00:09:56.580
two rebellions, and threw back two invasions
by the Storm King, Durran the Third, and one

00:09:56.580 --> 00:09:59.340
by King Greydon Gardener of the Reach.

00:09:59.340 --> 00:10:05.649
As Nymeria grew aged and infirm, the armies
of House Martell were commanded by her heirs.

00:10:05.649 --> 00:10:11.220
When she at last died, Nymeria was succeeded
as Princess of Dorne by her eldest daughter

00:10:11.220 --> 00:10:17.200
by Lord Mors Martell, not by her only son
by Ser Davos Dayne, for Dorne had come to

00:10:17.200 --> 00:10:20.720
adopt many of the laws and customs of the
Rhoynar.

00:10:20.720 --> 00:10:25.570
The Dornish revere Nymeria as the founder
of their realm, and her descendants in House

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:29.770
Martell continue to rule Dorne through the
present day.

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:34.980
As a result, "Nymeria" actually became a common
name in Dorne (comparable to how "Brandon"

00:10:34.980 --> 00:10:40.140
is a very common name in the North, after
their founder, Brandon the Builder).

00:10:40.140 --> 00:10:46.800
Oberyn Martell - himself a direct descendant
of Nymeria, warrior-queen of the Rhoynar - named

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:49.690
one of his own daughters Nymeria.

00:10:49.690 --> 00:10:55.430
Nymeria's fame also spread across Westeros:
even young Arya Stark, fascinated with legends

00:10:55.430 --> 00:11:00.370
about this warrior-queen, chose to name her
direwolf "Nymeria".

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:05.950
Nymeria's life inspired the books Ten Thousand
Ships and The Loves of Queen Nymeria, as well

00:11:05.950 --> 00:11:10.310
as the upcoming Game of Thrones prequel series
10,000 Ships.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:16.000
Legendary characters such as Princess Nymeria,
legendary battles such as 300 Valyrian dragons

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.911
fighting Rhoynar and their water wizards,
as well as many battles warrior-queen Nymeria

00:11:20.911 --> 00:11:27.320
fought in Dorne, defeating 6 Dornish kings,
all of that and more this Game of Thrones

00:11:27.320 --> 00:11:28.320
prequel show, 10,000 Ships, will bring.

00:11:28.320 --> 00:11:29.740
Let me know your thoughts about all of this
in the comment section down below.

00:11:29.740 --> 00:11:33.670
Thank you so much for watching and I hope
to see you in the next one.

00:11:33.670 --> 00:11:34.139
Peace!

